{
  "description": "What a String data property's defaultValue means, for every reader: the code generators (sjui / kjui / rjui — JsonUIShared::StringLiterals.default_text and TypeConverterCore#normalize_data_property) and the dynamic runtimes (SwiftJsonUI and KotlinJsonUI DynamicView). Each row is written by hand, not computed. Canonical copy: jsonui-cli shared/core/string_default_vectors.json; SwiftJsonUI and KotlinJsonUI vendor it byte-identical for their tests (the COPIES list in their CI).",
  "spellingsDescription": "A String defaultValue as written in the layout, and the text it means. bare (canonical): the text as written. '' : empty. \"…\" : JSON's escapes; when they do not parse, the text between the quotes as written. '…' : the text between the quotes as written. A raw control character or a lone surrogate is not JSON either.",
  "spellings": [
    {
      "name": "bare",
      "spelling": "Hello",
      "text": "Hello"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare, every special character",
      "spelling": "Say \"hi\" \\ $x \\(z) ${y} `b` it's",
      "text": "Say \"hi\" \\ $x \\(z) ${y} `b` it's"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare, a quote at one end only",
      "spelling": "\"lead",
      "text": "\"lead"
    },
    {
      "name": "bare, an apostrophe at one end only",
      "spelling": "trail'",
