  "platformsDescription": "A defaultValue written per platform ({\"swift\": …, \"kotlin\": …, \"typescript\": …}). A platform it names gets its value (a String value read as in spellings; swift reads the swiftui mode, kotlin the compose mode). A platform it does not name gets the class's vocabulary value — \"\" / 0 / 0.0 / false / [] — or no value (null here) for an optional, and the code generators warn naming the layout, the property and the platform. A dictionary whose keys are not all platform names is a value, the same on every platform. warnFor lists the platforms a code generator warns for.",
  "platforms": [
    {
      "name": "String given for swift and kotlin",
      "class": "String",
      "defaultValue": {
        "swift": "eager",
        "kotlin": "lazy"
      },
      "expect": {
        "swift": "eager",
        "kotlin": "lazy",
        "typescript": ""
      },
      "warnFor": [
        "typescript"
      ]
    },
    {
